      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is more than double the maximum daily dose, and it's in the range that can cause acute liver injury. Confirming the order doesn't change that risk, and you haven't given a clinical rationale that would justify it.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within limits.** I can enter 1000 mg PO every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day) or 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) right away.\n- **Check the intent.** If this came from a verbal order, a handoff, or a template, it may be a typo, such as 300 mg or 1000 mg.\n- **Escalate if you think it's intentional.** Talk to your attending and pharmacy. If they approve a dose outside standard limits, it should go through your hospital's override process with the rationale documented.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it now."
      }
